cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SOLARAEUS: Certified Incremental SOLWEIG-Compatible Urban Thermal-Comfort Simulation"
abstract: >-
  A CPU/GPU research prototype that reuses cached pedestrian-level mean radiant
  temperature fields after local 3D building edits, while guaranteeing a
  computable, model-specific error bound B_T(x) on every reused grid cell.
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - urban microclimate
  - mean radiant temperature
  - SOLWEIG
  - UTCI
  - certified incremental computation
  - error bounds
  - GPU ray tracing
authors:
  - family-names: "SOLARAEUS contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ayushsingh08-ds/solaraeus"
